title Two rungs regain an invariant, and the baseline moves inside the lap
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds first, send the increment
think The queue named seat_note the head at 504 over forty-three rungs, opening three declarations -- the first lift of the arc that would cost a widening. That price earned a read before a line moved.
think Read what the three widenings actually were. sh tools/fixtures/ladder_reach_visibility_scan.sh seat_note named a private note_path in reclaim.rye, reckon.rye, and abandon.rye. Reading those three showed each is already a three-line stub delegating to ladder_checks.note_path, and forty-one sibling rungs publish exactly the same stub. So the widening was a uniformity gap rather than a surface expansion.
think Read the four rungs whose seat_note body differs from the forty-three. Hashing split them two and two: entrust.rye and taper.rye take value: u8 and write one byte where the forty-three take a bytes slice -- a real difference of signature. confer.rye and revoke.rye write the identical body minus one line, the assert that a note carries a suffix.
think Checked every seat_note call site in confer.rye and revoke.rye before touching the assert. All eighteen pass a real suffix -- .given, .held, .offered, .words, .pruning, .kept, .pruned -- and the one empty string in each is the bytes argument rather than the suffix. So restoring the invariant changes no behavior and refuses nothing that runs today.
think Restored assert(suffix.len >= 1) in both, scoped to the seat_note function since the same two-line opening appears twice in each file. The family read 43 identical, then 45. confer.rye still stays home: ladder_checks imports it, so it stands below the fold line and folding it would have the harness reach back through a rung it already reaches for.
think Published the four private note_path stubs, which brought REACH_OK from widens=4 to widens=0 at fall=531, and freed read_words at the same time -- it read widens=3 before the publishes and reads widens=0 after.
think Lifted the body into caravan/ladder_checks.rye as pub fn seat_note(comptime rung: type, io: std.Io, domain: []const u8, suffix: []const u8, bytes: []const u8) rung.NoteError!void, prefixing three symbols. Dir is already declared in the harness, so Dir.cwd() stands unchanged. Stubbed forty-four rungs, excluding the harness, confer.rye, entrust.rye, and taper.rye by name.
think The realized fall first read 514 against the carry measured at the head of the lap, disagreeing with the predicted 531. Rather than book a red or adjust the prose, rebuilt the pre-fold tree in a scratch copy -- the same forty-four bodies, the restored asserts, the published stubs -- and measured it: 71,393. The fold's true fall is 71,393 - 70,862 = 531 exactly.
obs Prediction met measurement to the digit for the seventh lap running, read against the tree the fold actually ran on. Carry 71,393 -> 70,862, a fall of exactly 531; delegates 3,073 -> 3,117; bodies 18,170 -> 18,171; distinct 7,967 -> 7,968; families 705 -> 704 as the two-member confer/revoke family dissolved into the forty-five; ceiling down to 70,868.
obs The 17-line rise from 71,376 to 71,393 is family accounting rather than four added lines: confer and revoke left a two-member family at thirteen lines and joined a forty-five-member family at fifteen, and carry counts copies beyond the first.
obs First firing of a lantern. A lap that edits bodies before folding them must re-baseline the carry, and nothing enforces it -- only the prediction disagreeing with the measurement caught it. Six laps of predicting the fall before moving a line is what made the disagreement legible at all. A second firing earns a tool; one firing earns this line.
obs The widening the queue priced was a uniformity gap the meter counts honestly as a widening. Four rungs kept private what forty-one published, and every one of the four was already a delegating stub. Reading what a number is made of turned a cost into a ratchet, and the lift came back free.
obs The dropped invariant is the more useful find. Two rungs ran without the assert their forty-three siblings keep, and no witness noticed because the assert never fires on any call site that exists. It was found by asking why a body differed rather than by a guard, which is the arc's habit of reading outliers earning its keep in a place a meter could not reach.
obs No red booked. Nothing wrong shipped and no claim was made on the stale baseline; the disagreement was caught and resolved by measurement before any prose was written.
