file crux/REMEMBER.md the Now block refilled, the uniformity gap named, and the baseline lantern recorded
recommend keep-going read_words at forty-three identical bodies over forty-five declarations by fifteen lines -- 504 by realized fall, zero widening, free because publishing the four note_path stubs paid its cost too. Behind it read_count 462, also free. elder_waits returns the same 504 and door_admits 462 while each opens all forty-three, so both stay the cheapest-looking rows that cost the most. Watch the baseline: if a lap edits bodies before folding them a second time, the re-baseline becomes a tool rather than a habit.
